Thanks for the solid work. I amended your commit with a few fixes:

- `Enter` on an item that wraps a link did not follow the link. The controller calls `click()` on the item `<div>`, and the `<a>` inside it never receives that click. `Command:Item` now takes `as="a"`, like `Item` and `DropdownMenu:Item` already do, so the whole item is the link. Link items get `tabindex="-1"`, so Tab does not walk through every item. The README has a new "Links" example.

- Items added after the controller connected (for example by a Turbo Stream) had no id, so `aria-activedescendant` was empty. Ids are now given in `itemTargetConnected()`.

- Hovering the half-visible item at the bottom of the list scrolled the list. `cmdk` does not scroll on pointer selection, so `highlight()` no longer scrolls either.

Each of these changes has a spec that failed before the fix.
